Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 17:03:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] aggregate_copy_forward: reject use-before-def rewrites in
 store-only forwarding
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

forward_store_only_temporaries redirects pre-memcpy uses of a temporary
onto the memcpy destination — but never checked that the destination is
DEFINED at those points. The sret pointer is typically loaded from its
alloca immediately before the memcpy, so rewriting an earlier Store to
address through it emitted a store through an uninitialized register
(movl $1234, (%r11) with dead %r11 -> SIGSEGV in struct_by_value).

Fail-closed dominance check: the destination's def site must precede the
FIRST use of the root inside the copy's block (same-block case), or be
an entry-block def (only block guaranteed to dominate all others);
parameters (no def site) are always live. Anything else is dropped.

PROOF: struct_by_value 0 77 2.5 1234, exit 0 (was SIGSEGV).
Regressions 142->143.
