The dead-field-store analysis modeled a variable-offset GEP as offset 0.
A loop reading exp[i] therefore only 'read' bytes [0,4) of the array;
every initializing store at offset >= 4 was declared dead and deleted
(simd_vhaddps: FAIL lane 1, 7/8 expected-value stores removed).

Offsets are now Option<i64>: variable GEPs and phi merges of differing
offsets are None. A load through an unknown offset conservatively reads
the ENTIRE aggregate; a store through an unknown offset is never dead.
This is the standard may-alias lattice (known-offset / unknown-offset /
escaped) — collapsing unknown to 0 was unsound by construction.

Regressions 143->151 (fixes simd_vhaddps, simd_vpermilvar256,
simd_blendv256, simd_avx2_256, set_epi32_order, gvn_param_alloca_load,
hash_narrow_chain, reduction_two_sums).
